# Spring Boot defaults

Follow the **existing** project layout, Boot version, and error contract when they already exist. These defaults apply only to new Spring Boot code.

This rule does **not** control git. Commit and push follow `todo.md` phases / `git-auto-commit-push`. Before marking a task complete, run `./mvnw test` (or `mvn test`). Use `./mvnw verify` when the phase includes slice or integration tests.

If the repo uses a `Backend` folder, the Spring Boot module lives there. Do not add a second Java root at the repo root.

Align JPA entities with `ERD.md` at the project root. Do not add tables or entities that are not in the ERD.

Use hexagonal, Modulith, or a `{success, data, error}` envelope **only** when the user asks or the project already uses them.

## Layout

Default packages are **by feature**, with layered responsibilities inside the feature.

❌ BAD — global technical layers

```
com.example.app.controller.UserController
com.example.app.service.UserService
com.example.app.repository.UserRepository
```

✅ GOOD — feature packages

```
com.example.app.user.api            # controllers, request/response records
com.example.app.user.domain         # services, entities, domain exceptions
com.example.app.user.infrastructure # repositories, HTTP clients
com.example.app.common              # cross-cutting config and exception advice
```

## Controllers and services

Controllers: HTTP only. `@Valid` on request bodies. Never return JPA entities. Never inject repositories.

Services: business logic and `@Transactional`. Constructor injection only (`final` + `@RequiredArgsConstructor`).

Repositories: data access only.

❌ BAD — logic, entity, and repository in the controller; field injection

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/users")
public class UserController {
    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;

    @PostMapping
    public User create(@RequestBody User user) {
        if (user.getEmail() == null || !user.getEmail().contains("@")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid email");
        }
        return userRepository.save(user);
    }
}
```

✅ GOOD — lean controller, DTO records, service owns rules

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/users")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class UserController {
    private final UserService userService;

    @PostMapping
    public ResponseEntity<UserResponse> create(@Valid @RequestBody UserCreateRequest request) {
        UserResponse body = userService.create(request);
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(body);
    }
}

public record UserCreateRequest(@Email @NotBlank String email) {}

public record UserResponse(Long id, String email) {
    public static UserResponse from(User user) {
        return new UserResponse(user.getId(), user.getEmail());
    }
}

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class UserService {
    private final UserRepository userRepository;

    @Transactional
    public UserResponse create(UserCreateRequest request) {
        User saved = userRepository.save(User.from(request));
        return UserResponse.from(saved);
    }
}
```

## Build and config

Inherit `spring-boot-starter-parent` or the Boot BOM. Do not invent dependency versions. Do not pin a Boot version the project does not already use.

Store settings in `application.yml` / env vars. Never hardcode secrets. Never commit `.env`.

Group related settings in a `@ConfigurationProperties` **record** with `@Validated`. Register it via `@EnableConfigurationProperties` or `@ConfigurationPropertiesScan`. Do not use `@Data` on property types. Prefer `Duration` / `DataSize` over raw millis.

❌ BAD — hardcoded URL, invented version, mutable `@Data` properties

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
  <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
  <version>3.2.11</version>
</dependency>
```

```java
@Service
public class ExternalClient {
    public String call() {
        return rest.getForObject("https://api.example.com", String.class);
    }
}

@Configuration
@ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "app.client")
@Data
public class ClientProperties {
    private String baseUrl;
    private int timeoutMs;
    private String apiToken;
}
```

✅ GOOD — BOM-managed deps, typed record, YAML with units

```xml
<parent>
  <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
  <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
  <version>${revision}</version>
  <relativePath/>
</parent>
<dependencies>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
  </dependency>
</dependencies>
```

```yaml
app:
  client:
    base-url: https://api.example.com
    timeout: 5s
```

```java
@ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "app.client")
@Validated
public record ClientProperties(
    @NotBlank String baseUrl,
    @NotNull Duration timeout
) {}

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ExternalClient {
    private final ClientProperties properties;
    private final RestClient restClient;

    public String call() {
        return restClient.get()
            .uri(properties.baseUrl())
            .retrieve()
            .body(String.class);
    }
}
```

Keep `${revision}` / parent version equal to the project's current Boot version. Do not "upgrade" it in passing.

## API and errors

One error policy per API. Default for new APIs: RFC 9457. Return `ProblemDetail`, not a custom `{status, message}` record. Keep domain exceptions free of HTTP types unless the project already uses `@ResponseStatus`.

❌ BAD — ad-hoc body, HTTP types on the domain, success envelope invented for a new API

```yaml
# missing spring.mvc.problemdetails.enabled
```

```java
@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
public class UserNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public UserNotFoundException(Long id) {
        super("Could not find user " + id);
    }
}

@ControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    @ExceptionHandler(UserNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>> handle(UserNotFoundException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(404).body(Map.of(
            "success", false,
            "message", ex.getMessage()
        ));
    }
}
```

✅ GOOD — Problem Details + domain exception without HTTP

```yaml
spring:
  mvc:
    problemdetails:
      enabled: true
```

```java
public class UserNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public UserNotFoundException(Long id) {
        super("Could not find user " + id);
    }
}

@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler extends ResponseEntityExceptionHandler {

    @ExceptionHandler(UserNotFoundException.class)
    public ProblemDetail handleNotFound(UserNotFoundException ex) {
        ProblemDetail problem = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, ex.getMessage());
        problem.setTitle("Not Found");
        problem.setType(URI.create("https://api.example.com/errors/user-not-found"));
        problem.setProperty("errorCode", "USER_NOT_FOUND");
        return problem;
    }
}
```

## Logging and tests

SLF4J + `@Slf4j`. Parameterized messages only. Never `System.out`.

- Unit: `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`, `@Mock`, `@InjectMocks`. No `MockitoAnnotations.openMocks`.
- Slice: `@WebMvcTest` / `@DataJpaTest` with `@MockitoBean` (not `@MockBean`).
- Integration: `@SpringBootTest` plus Testcontainers. Do not call `@WebMvcTest` an integration test.
- Name tests `method_condition_expected`. Prefer AssertJ.

❌ BAD — string concat, manual Mockito init, `@MockBean`, wrong test type name

```java
public void process(String data) {
    System.out.println("Processing data: " + data);
    log.info("Processing data: " + data);
}

class UserServiceTest {
    @Mock UserRepository users;
    @InjectMocks UserService service;

    @BeforeEach
    void setUp() {
        MockitoAnnotations.openMocks(this);
    }

    @Test
    void testFind() { ... }
}

@WebMvcTest(UserController.class)
class UserControllerIntegrationTest {
    @MockBean UserService userService;
}
```

✅ GOOD — placeholders, MockitoExtension, slice vs unit, `@MockitoBean`

```java
@Service
@Slf4j
public class UserService {
    public void process(String data) {
        log.info("Processing data: {}", data);
    }
}

@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class UserServiceTest {
    @Mock UserRepository users;
    @InjectMocks UserService service;

    @Test
    void findById_whenMissing_throwsNotFound() {
        when(users.findById(2L)).thenReturn(Optional.empty());
        assertThatThrownBy(() -> service.findById(2L))
            .isInstanceOf(UserNotFoundException.class);
    }
}

@WebMvcTest(UserController.class)
class UserControllerTest {
    @Autowired MockMvc mockMvc;
    @MockitoBean UserService userService;

    @Test
    void create_withValidRequest_returns201() throws Exception { ... }
}
```
